 86    H TYP=FUL$AUT=A. Negret and B. Singh$CIT=NDS 203, 283 (2025)$            
 86  2 H CUT=20-Jan-2025$                                                       
 86   C  TITL$Nuclear Structure and Decay data for A=86 isobars                 
 86   c  AUTH$A. Negret{+1} and B. Singh{+2,|:}                                 
 86   c  INST${+1}Horia Hulubei National Institute for Physics                  
 86  #c       and Nuclear Engineering, Reactorului 30,                          
 86  #c       Magurele, Romania                                                 
 86  #c       {+2}Department of Physics and Astronomy,                          
 86  #c       McMaster University,                                              
 86  #c       Hamilton, Ontario L8S 4M1, Canada.                                
 86   c  ABST$Experimental nuclear spectroscopic data are evaluated for 14      
 86  2c  known nuclides of mass number A=86 (Ga, Ge, As, Se, Br, Kr, Rb, Sr, Y, 
 86  3c  Zr, Nb, Mo, Tc, Ru). Detailed evaluated information is presented for   
 86  4c  each reaction and decay. Recommended values combining all available    
 86  5c  data are provided for the spectroscopic properties of each level,      
 86  6c  |g-ray, and decay radiation. Limited level and gamma information is    
 86  7c  available for {+86}Ga (ground state and one excited level), {+86}Ge    
 86  8c  (six levels), and {+86}As (ten excited states), with their respective  
 86  9c  |b{+-} decays poorly known. Fairly detailed level and gamma data are   
 86  Ac  available for {+86}Se, {+86}Br, {+86}Kr, {+86}Rb, {+86}Sr and {+86}Y   
 86  Bc  nuclei. The decay of {+86}Br to {+86}Kr has recently been studied by   
 86  Cc  gamma spectroscopy (2016Ur04) and by TAGS technique (2017Ri08), the    
 86  Dc  latter suggesting that many additional levels in {+86}Kr exist which   
 86  Ec  have not been detected in high-resolution |g-ray spectroscopy. The     
 86  Fc  |g-ray spectra in 2016Ur04 were valid up to E|g=4 MeV, whereas the     
 86  Gc  Q(|b) value of 7.63 MeV for {+86}Br permits population of high-energy  
 86  Hc  levels. For {+86}Zr, {+86}Nb and {+86}Mo, the data are available for   
 86  Ic  mostly the high-spin states, as the decays of {+86}Nb, {+86}Mo, and    
 86  Jc  {+86}Tc, which could populate low-spin levels, are not known well. For 
 86  Kc  {+86}Tc, only four levels are known from the decay of an isomeric      
 86  Lc  activity in {+86}Tc. In addition, decay of {+86}Tc with g.s. J|p=(0+)  
 86  Mc  to 0+ g.s. in {+86}Mo could involve superallowed |b transition, which  
 86  Nc  has been pursued experimentally in detail. For {+86}Ru only the        
 86  Oc  isotopic identification is established, with its half-life and decay   
 86  Pc  modes unknown. The evaluated data in this work supersede data in       
 86  Qc  earlier ENSDF evaluation of A=86 nuclei by 2015Ne01, where the         
 86  Rc  literature cutoff date was November 30, 2014.                          
 86   c  CUT$Literature available up to January 20, 2025 has been consulted,    
 86  2c  with the help of the primary bibliographic source, the NSR database    
 86  3c  (2011Pr03) available at Brookhaven National Laboratory web page:       
 86  #c  www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/                                                  
 86   c  COMM$The statistical analysis of |g-ray data and deduced level schemes 
 86  2c  is carried out using a suite of computer codes available at the        
 86  3c  IAEA-Nuclear Data Sheets website: www-nds.iaea.org/public/ensdf_pgm.   
 86  4c  The direct feedings to excited states in |b{+-} and |e decays have     
 86  5c  generally been computed from I(|g+ce) intensity balances at each       
 86  6c  level. The BetaShape-v2.4 code (2019Mo35) was used to deduce log|      
 86  7c  {ift} values and average |b energies in |b{+-} and |e decay datasets.  
 86  8c  Theoretical total conversion coefficients were calculated using the    
 86  9c  BrIcc-v2.3e code (2008Ki07) for frozen-orbit option. In cases where    
 86  Ac  weighted averaging procedures have been used, the assigned uncertainty 
 86  Bc  in the result is generally not lower than the lowest uncertainty       
 86  Cc  amongst the data points used in the process.                           
 86   c  CIT$NDS 203, 283 (2025)                                                
 86   c  ACKN$Earlier evaluations (2015Ne01, 2001Si43, 1997Ki04, 1988Mu14,      
 86  2c  1978Te01), and compilations of recent articles in the XUNDL database   
 86  3c  provided valuable resources for the present work. The evaluators are   
 86  4c  grateful to reviewers of this work at different stages of this         
 86  5c  evaluation, and to the personnel at the NNDC, Brookhaven National      
 86   c  PERM$|: Deceased PERM$ Corresponding author: A. Negret,                
 86   c  negret@nipne.ro.  FUND$ A. Negret's work was supported by Euratom      
 86  2c  research and training program 2014-2018 under grant agreement No       
 86  3c  { 847552. b}. Singh's work was partially supported through a contract  
 86  4c  from Brookhaven National Laboratory, Upton, N.Y., USA.                 

