 86GA c  1997Be70: {+86}Ga produced and identified in {+9}Be({+238}U,F)         
 86GA2c  reaction at E=750 MeV/nucleon at GSI. Identification by                
 86GA3c  Fragment-Recoil Separator (FRS) and time-of-flight. A total of four    
 86GA4c  events were assigned to {+86}Ga.                                       
 86GA c  2013Mi19, 2014Gr03: proton beam was provided by the Oak Ridge          
 86GA2c  Isochronous Cyclotron (ORIC) at the HRIBF-ORNL facility.               
 86GA3c  Target=UC{-x}.  Mass analyzed ions of {+86}Ga were extracted using     
 86GA4c  Resonant Ionization Laser Ion Source (RILIS). Pure {+86}Ga beam was    
 86GA5c  then sent to the Low-energy Radioactive Ion Beam Spectroscopy Station  
 86GA6c  (LeRIBSS) and implanted in a moving tape collector (MTC). Measured     
 86GA7c  E|g, I|g, E|b, |b|g-coin, n|g-coin, half-life of {+86}Ga, P{-n},       
 86GA8c  P{-2n} using two HPGe Clover detectors, two plastic scintillation      
 86GA9c  counters for |b, and an array of 48 {+3}He ionization chambers for     
 86GA9c  neutron detection.  Comparison of measured half-life, P{-1n} and       
 86GAAc  P{-2n} with predictions from several calculations such as FRDM+QRPA,   
 86GABc  FRDM+QRPA2, DF3a+CQRPA, DF3a+CQRPA+fragmentation of |b strength;       
 86GACc  FRDM=finite range droplet model, CQRPA=continuum quasiparticle random  
 86GADc  phase approximation; DF=density functional.                            
 86GA c  2014XuZZ (thesis): {+86}Ga produced in {+9}Be({+238}U,F), E=345        
 86GA2c  MeV/nucleon, and separated using BigRIPS and ZeroDegree spectrometers  
 86GA3c  at RIBF-RIKEN facility, followed by |b and |g counting using EURICA    
 86GA4c  array for |g rays. Measured half-life of decay of {+86}Ga by ({+86}Ga  
 86GA5c  implants)|b-correlated events, and by |b(215.5|g)-coin decay curve.    
 86GA6c  According to Fig. 3.7 showing a plot of yields of different isotopes,  
 86GA7c  a large number of events were assigned to {+86}Ga.                     
 86GA c  2023Yo04,2019Yo03,2020ToZY: {+86}Ga produced in the {+9}Be({+238}U,F)  
 86GA2c  reaction at E({+238}U)=345 MeV/nucleon on a 4-mm thick {+9}Be          
 86GA3c  production target followed by the separation and identification of     
 86GA4c  fragments of interest by A/Q on the basis of magnetic rigidity B|r,    
 86GA5c  time-of-flight (tof) and energy loss (|DE) using the BigRIPS in-flight 
 86GA6c  separator, plastic scintillation counters, and position-sensitive      
 86GA7c  parallel-plate avalanche counters (PPACs), finally implanted into      
 86GA8c  active stoppers: AIDA in one run (described in 2020ToZY), and WAS3Abi  
 86GA9c  in a second run (2019Yo03), both consisting of double-sided silicon    
 86GAbc  strip detectors (DSSDs) at the RIBF-RIKEN facility. Measured E|g, I|g, 
 86GAcc  E|b, I|b, E(n), I(n), ion-|b correlations, (neutron)ion-|b-coin,       
 86GAdc  n|b|g-coin, (2n)|b|g-coin, |g|g-coin using two clover HPGe detectors   
 86GAec  for |g rays, and the BRIKEN detector consisting of 140 proportional    
 86GAfc  counters filled with {+3}He gas for neutrons.  Deduced half-life of    
 86GAgc  {+86}Ga decay, %|b{+-}n or P1n, %|b{+-}2n or P2n, and the decays of    
 86GAhc  {+86}Ga to {+86}Ge, {+85}Ge, and {+84}Ge. Also, deduced a 0.32-|ms     
 86GAic  isomer in {+86}Ga                                                      
 86GA c  Evaluators' note: 2019Yo03 and 2020ToZY provide results from two       
 86GA2c  different runs carried out at BRIKEN-RIKEN facility, with independent  
 86GA3c  analysis methodology (per e-mail communications with J.L. Tain and A.  
 86GA4c  Tolosa-Delgado, January 14-18, 2023). 2023Yo04 presents common results 
 86GA5c  from the two runs superseding the previous reports.                    
