 86GE c  1994Be24: {+86}Ge produced and identified in Pb({+238}U,F) reaction at 
 86GE2c  E=750 MeV/nucleon at the SIS synchrotron, GSI. Identification using the
 86GE3c  B|r-|DE-tof method and FRS separator                                   
 86GE c  2013Ma22: proton beam was provided by the Oak Ridge Isochronous        
 86GE2c  Cyclotron (ORIC) at the HRIBF-ORNL facility. Target={+238}UC{-x}.      
 86GE3c  Fission fragments were ionized to charge state +1 then purified using  
 86GE4c  H{-2}S gas, a mass pre-separator and electromagnetic separation. The   
 86GE5c  purified beams were then sent to the Low-energy Radioactive Ion Beam   
 86GE6c  Spectroscopy Station (LeRIBSS) and implanted in a moving tape collector
 86GE7c  (MTC). Measured E|g, I|g, E|b, |b|g-coin, half-life of {+86}Ge g.s.    
 86GE8c  using two plastic scintillation counters and four HPGe detectors.      
 86GE9c  Comparison with the gross theory of |b decay, the finite-range droplet 
 86GEAc  model and the continuum quasiparticle random-phase approximation.      
 86GE c  2014XuZZ (thesis): {+86}Ge produced in {+9}Be({+238}U,F),              
 86GE2c  E=345 MeV/nucleon, and separated using BigRIPS and ZeroDegree          
 86GE3c  spectrometers at RIBF-RIKEN facility, followed by |b and |g counting   
 86GE4c  using EURICA array for |g rays. Measured half-life of decay of {+86}Ge 
 86GE5c  by ({+86}Ge implants)|b-correlated events, and by |b(215.5|g)-coin     
 86GE6c  decay curve. According to Fig. 3.7 showing a plot of yields of         
 86GE7c  different isotopes, a large number of events were assigned to          
 86GE8c  {+86}Ge.                                                               
 86GE c  Mass measurement: 2006Ha62                                             
 86GE c  Theoretical structure calculations:                                    
 86GE c  2022Su20: calculated potential energy surfaces in (|b,|g) plane,       
 86GE2c  isoscalar giant monopole, quadrupole, hexadecupole resonance           
 86GE3c  structures, transition densities, single neutron levels, with          
 86GE4c  evidence for monopole-quadrupole-hexadecupole coupling. Quasiparticle  
 86GE5c  finite amplitude method (QFAM) based on the covariant density          
 86GE6c  functional (CDFT) theory DD-ME2 and a separable pairing force.         
 86GE c  2020Ab05: calculated potential energy surface (PES) in (|b{-2},|g)     
 86GE2c  plane, S(2n), neutron-, proton-, and charge-radii, |b and |g           
 86GE3c  deformations, shape coexistence using the relativistic                 
 86GE4c  Hartree-Bogoliubov formalism with density-dependent zero- and          
 86GE5c  finite-range and DD-PC1 interactions.                                  
 86GE c  2017No04: calculated mean-field potential energy surfaces in (|b,|g)   
 86GE2c  plane using the Gogny-D1M EDF, and the IBM, level energies and B(E2)   
 86GE3c  of low-lying 0+, 2+ and 4+ states, fraction of intruder configuration  
 86GE4c  in 0+ states, spectroscopic quadrupole moments of 2+ states,           
 86GE5c  |r{+2}(E0) using Interacting boson model (IBM) with self-consistent    
 86GE6c  mean-field calculation based on the Gogny-D1M energy density           
 86GE7c  functional, with mean-field energy surface from constrained            
 86GE8c  Hartree-Fock-Bogoliubov (HFB) method.                                  
 86GE c  2013Si25: calculated levels, J|p, yrast and excited bands, intrinsic   
 86GE2c  and spectroscopic quadrupole moments, B(E2), deformation parameters    
 86GE3c  |b and |g, potential energy surface contours in (|b,|g) plane using    
 86GE4c  algebraic pseudo-SU(3) model, and shell model.                         
