 86GE c  2023Yo04,2019Yo03,2020ToZY: {+86}Ga produced in the                    
 86GE2c  {+9}Be({+238}U,F) reaction at E({+238}U)=345 MeV/nucleon               
 86GE3c  on a 4-mm thick {+9}Be production target                               
 86GE4c  followed by the separation and identification of fragments of interest 
 86GE5c  by A/Q on the basis of magnetic rigidity B|r, time-of-flight (tof) and 
 86GE6c  energy loss (|DE) using the BigRIPS in-flight separator, plastic       
 86GE7c  scintillation counters, and position-sensitive parallel-plate          
 86GE8c  avalanche counters (PPACs), finally implanted into active stoppers:    
 86GE9c  AIDA in one run (described in 2020ToZY), and WAS3Abi in a second run   
 86GEac  (2019Yo03), both consisting of double-sided                            
 86GEbc  silicon strip detectors (DSSDs) at the RIBF-RIKEN                      
 86GEcc  facility. Measured E|g, I|g, E|b, I|b, E(n), I(n), ion-|b correlations,
 86GEdc  (neutron)ion-|b-coin, n|b|g-coin, (2n)|b|g-coin, |g|g-coin using two   
 86GEec  clover HPGe detectors for |g rays, and the BRIKEN detector consisting  
 86GEfc  of 140 proportional counters filled with {+3}He gas for neutrons.      
 86GEgc  Deduced half-life of {+86}Ga decay, %|b{+-}n or P1n, %|b{+-}2n or P2n, 
 86GEhc  and the decays of {+86}Ga to {+86}Ge, {+85}Ge, and {+84}Ge. Also,      
 86GEic  deduced a 0.32-|ms isomer in {+86}Ga                                   
 86GE c  Evaluators' note: 2019Yo03 and 2020ToZY provide results from two       
 86GE2c  different runs carried out at BRIKEN-RIKEN facility, with              
