 86AS c  {+86}As produced and identified by 1973Kr06 (also 1974KrZG,1975Kr08)   
 86AS2c  in neutron-induced fission of {+235}U followed by chemical separation  
 86AS3c  and half-life measurement. Earlier studies                             
 86AS4c  (1966To02,1967De01,1968To18,1968To19,1969WaZS) reported decays of mixed
 86AS5c  {+85}As and {+86}As activities by observing the decay of its           
 86AS6c  descendants {+86}Se and {+86}Br, and by counting of delayed neutrons   
 86AS4c  after separation of arsenic sample from other fission products of      
 86AS5c  {+235}U. A 2-s half-life reported for this mixture most likely         
 86AS6c  corresponded to {+85}As activity                                       
 86AS c  T{-1/2} and %|b{+-}n measurements: 2013Ma22, 1993Ru01, 1978Cr03,       
 86AS2c  1973Kr06 (also 1974KrZG,1975Kr08)                                      
 86AS c  Precise mass measurements: 2008Ha23 (Penning-trap method), 2008Su19    
 86AS2c  (also 2010Li02) (isochronous mass spectrometry)                        
 86AS c  2013Ma22: 50-MeV proton beam provided by the Oak Ridge Isochronous     
 86AS2c  Cyclotron (ORIC) at the HRIBF-ORNL facility incident on {+238}UC{-x}.  
 86AS3c  Fission fragments were ionized to charge state +1 then purified using  
 86AS4c  H{-2}S gas, a mass pre-separator and electromagnetic separation. The   
 86AS5c  purified beams were then sent to the Low-energy Radioactive Ion Beam   
 86AS6c  Spectroscopy Station (LeRIBSS) and implanted in a moving tape collector
 86AS7c  (MTC). Measured E|g, I|g, E|b, |b|g-coin, half-life of {+86}As g.s.    
 86AS8c  using two plastic scintillation counters and four HPGe detectors.      
 86AS9c  Comparison with the gross theory of |b decay, the finite-range droplet 
 86ASAc  model and the continuum quasiparticle random-phase approximation.      
 86AS c  2020ToZY: {+87}Ge produced in {+9}Be({+238}U,F), E=345 MeV/nucleon;    
 86AS2c  followed by separation of fragments by A/Q and Z using BigRIPS and     
 86AS3c  ZeroDegree spectrometers at RIBF-RIKEN facility through measurements of
 86AS4c  time-of-flight (tof), magnetic rigidity (B|r) and energy loss (|DE).   
 86AS5c  Measured implanted ions, neutrons, |b, |g, |b(implants),               
 86AS6c  (implants)|b(1n)- and (implants)|b(2n)-correlations using BRIKEN       
 86AS7c  neutron counter with 140 {+3}He-filled proportional counters, AIDA     
 86AS8c  array of DSSSDs for implants and |b decays, two Clover HPGe detectors  
 86AS9c  for |g radiation, and two thick plastic scintillators; deduced         
 86ASAc  %|b{+-}n=33.5 {i16} and %|b{+-}2n=0.22 {i16} from simultaneous fits of 
 86ASBc  |b{+-}- and |b{+-}1n-decay curves, with uncertainties from Monte Carlo 
 86ASCc  method.                                                                
 86ASDc  Q({+87}Ge |b{+-}n decay)=7300 {i300} and Q({+88}Ge |b{+-}2n decay)=3300
 86ASEc  {i400} are estimated by evaluators from relevant mass excesses in      
 86ASFc  2021Wa16. T{-1/2}({+87}Ge |b{+-}n decay)=103.2 {i35} ms and            
 86ASGc  T{-1/2}({+88}Ge |b{+-}2n decay)=60.8 {i61} ms (|b-decay curve in       
 86ASHc  2014XuZZ).                                                             
 86AS c  No references for theoretical structure calculations in the            
 86AS2c  NSR database.                                                          
