 86SE c  {+86}Se nuclide first produced by 1960Sa05 who assigned a 16-s         
 86SE2c  activity incorrectly to {+87}Se. Confirmed identification is from      
 86SE3c  the work of 1973Ta19, and later studies 1974KrZG, 1975Hu02 and 1978Ze08
 86SE d  2002So13: measured production cross section in {+64}Ni({+86}Kr,X) at   
 86SE2d  25 MeV/nucleon                                                         
 86SE c  Precise mass measurements: 2008Ha23, 2008Su19                          
 86SE c  Theoretical structure calculations:                                    
 86SE c  2022No05, 2021No05, 2017No04: calculated potential energy surfaces in  
 86SE2c  (|b{-2},|b{-3}) plane, levels, J|p, B(E1), B(E2), B(E3), intruder      
 86SE3c  configuration in 0+ states, spectroscopic quadrupole moments of 2+     
 86SE4c  state, |r{+2}(E0) using interacting boson model with self-consistent   
 86SE5c  mean-field theory, based on the Gogny-D1M energy density functional.   
 86SE c  2021Co08: calculated total energy per nucleon for the prolate and      
 86SE2c  oblate solutions, deformation parameters |b{-2}, charge radius, charge 
 86SE3c  density, splittings between centroid energies of spin-orbit partner    
 86SE4c  multiplets using Hartree-Fock (HF) method with pairing effects by BCS  
 86SE5c  method, and Gogny type D1S and D1ST2a interactions containing          
 86SE6c  tensor terms.                                                          
 86SE c  2020Ab05: calculated potential energy surface in (|b{-2},|g) plane,    
 86SE2c  S(2n), neutron-, proton-, and charge-radii, |b and |g deformations     
 86SE3c  using relativistic Hartree-Bogoliubov formalism with density-dependent 
 86SE4c  zero- and finite-range NL3* and DD-PC1 interactions.                   
 86SE c  2018Th06: calculated levels, J|p, B(E2), potential energy curves,      
 86SE2c  collective wave function contours in (|b{-2},|g) plane, triaxiality,   
 86SE3c  deformation parameter |b{-2}, oblate and prolate potential energy curve
 86SE4c  minima using Algebraic collective model (ACM) with five-dimensional    
 86SE5c  collective Hamiltonian, and symmetry conserving configuration mixing   
 86SE6c  (SCCM) method with Gogny energy density functionals (EDF); and         
 86SE7c  Skyrme-Hartree-Fock model (SHF).                                       
 86SE c  2015Al12: calculated levels, J|p, B(E2), B(M1), |g branching ratios,   
 86SE2c  staggering parameter S(J) using interacting boson model (IBM-2), and   
 86SE3c  boson-fermion model (IBFM-2).                                          
 86SE c  2015Ma51: calculated levels, J|p, B(M1), B(E2) using shell model       
 86SE c  2013Si25: calculated levels, J|p, yrast and excited bands, intrinsic   
 86SE2c  and spectroscopic quadrupole moments, B(E2), deformation parameters    
 86SE3c  |b and |g, potential energy surface contours in (|b,|g) plane using    
 86SE4c  algebraic pseudo-SU(3) model, shell model with space outside {+78}Ni   
 86SE5c  core, and the particle and angular momentum symmetry conserving        
 86SE6c  beyond-mean field method with Gogny forces.                            
 86SE c  Other theory references for structure: 13 references retrieved from    
 86SE2c  the NSR database are listed in this dataset as 'document' records.     
 86SE d  Other theory references for structure: 2022Li53, 2022Su16, 2021So31,   
