 86SE c  2015Ma51: {+86}As beam produced in the neutron-induced fission of      
 86SE2c  {+235}U using recoil mass separator Lohengrin at the Institut          
 86SE3c  Laue-Langevin (ILL). Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |b|g-coin, |g|g(|q) 
 86SE4c  using a EUROBALL cluster detector with seven HPGe crystals, and three  
 86SE5c  plastic scintillators for |b detection. Comparison with shell-model    
 86SE6c  calculations                                                           
 86SE c  2015Ma61 (also 2015Ma25, 2013Ma22): {+86}As and {+86}Ge beams were     
 86SE2c  produced at the Holifield Radioactive Ion Beam facility (HRIBF) in     
 86SE3c  ORNL in U(p,F),E(p)=50 MeV, followed by separation of fragments using  
 86SE4c  an ion source and electromagnetic separation. The cocktail beam was    
 86SE5c  |?82% {+86}As and |?18% {+86}Ge. Radioactive ions were implanted on a  
 86SE6c  movable tape, with |g and |b radiations detected using four HPGe       
 86SE7c  clover detectors and two plastic scintillators.                        
 86SE8c  Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, and |b|g|g-coin.              
