 86SE c  2017El04: intermediate energy Coulomb excitation. Beam={+86}Se,        
 86SE2c  79 MeV/nucleon produced in {+9}Be({+96}Zr,X),E=120 MeV/nucleon using   
 86SE3c  K500 and K1200 coupled cyclotrons at NSCL-MSU facility, and fragments  
 86SE4c  separated using A1900 fragment separator. Target={+209}Bi,             
 86SE5c  246 mg/cm{+2} thick. Measured scattered particles using S800           
 86SE6c  spectrograph, E|g, I|g, (particle)|g-coin using CAESAR array           
 86SE7c  of 192 closely packed CsI(Na) crystals. Deduced cross section          
 86SE8c  for population of first 2+ state, and B(E2). Comparison with           
 86SE9c  shell-model calculations                                               
 86SE c  High-lying 2+ states were not observed by 2017El04, thus no feeding    
 86SE2c  correction was applied. In the literature, levels at 1399 (decaying    
 86SE3c  by 695 and 1399 |g rays) and 2208 keV (decaying by 1504 and 2208 |g    
 86SE4c  rays) are tentatively assigned as (2+). All the |g transitions were    
 86SE5c  below the sensitivity limit of the present work. 2017El04 estimated    
 86SE6c  that B(E2) would be reduced by at most 23% if feeding intensities      
 86SE7c  were to be taken from shell-model calculations.                        
