 86BR c  {+86}Br nuclide first produced in decay of {+86}Se by 1960Sa05 who     
 86BR2c  assigned a 16-s activity incorrectly to {+87}Se decay, instead of      
 86BR3c  correct assignment of {+86}Se to {+86}Br. Confirmed identification is  
 86BR4c  from the work of 1962St13, and several later studies.                  
 86BR c  A 4.5 s {I10} (possible isomeric) activity was assigned to {+86}Br by  
 86BR2c  1970Lu06 from the decay pattern of 1564|g in {+86}Kr, but the existence
 86BR3c  of this activity remains unconfirmed.                                  
 86BR c  Precise mass measurement using Penning-trap spectrometer: 2007Ra23     
 86BR c  2016Ur04: calculated levels, J|p, occupation of neutron and proton     
 86BR2c  orbitals using large-scale shell-model with the coupled-scheme code    
 86BR3c  NATHAN, in valence space outside the inert {+78}Ni core: |p1f{-5/2},   
 86BR4c  |p2p{-3/2}, |p2p{-1/2}, and |p1g{-9/2} proton orbitals; and |n2d{-5/2},
 86BR4c  |n3s{-1/2}, |n1g{-7/2}, |n2d{-3/2}, and |n1h{-11/2} neutron orbitals.  
 86BR cG E,RI$From {+86}Se |b{+-} decay (2016Ur04), unless otherwise            
 86BR2cG stated.                                                                
 86BR cG E(a),RI(a)$From {+235}U(n,F|g) (2016Ur04)                              
 86BR cG E(b),RI(b)$From {+208}Pb({+18}O,F|g) (2009Po10)                        
 86BR cG M$Assumed multipolarities are listed in square brackets for transitions
 86BR2cG with significant conversion coefficients.                              
 86BR cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g values.                                
 86BR cL J$Assignments are based mostly on shell-model calculations by 2016Ur04,
 86BR2cL and multiplets based on spherical configurations proposed for valence  
 86BR3cL protons and neutrons, and also configurations proposed by 2009Po10 for 
 86BR4cL selected levels. Arguments for each level are given under comments.    
 86BR5cL Note that 2016Ur04 give firm J|p assignments for many levels, but based
 86BR6cL on strong (and weak) rules for J|p assignments for ENSDF evaluations,  
 86BR7cL almost all the assignments are in parentheses in this dataset, with    
 86BR8cL the exception of firm 1+ for two strongly-populated levels in {+86}Se  
 86BR9cL |b{+-} decay from 0+ parent. Evaluators also differ in assignments for 
 86BRAcL many of the levels from those in 2016Ur04 where no shell-model         
 86BRBcL calculations are available.                                            
 86BRCcL The orbitals contributing near the Fermi level are: |p2p{-3/2},        
 86BRDcL |p1f{-5/2}{+-1} and |n2d{-5/2}, forming low-energy multiplets:         
 86BREcL |p2p{-3/2}~#|n2d{-5/2}, J|p=1- to 4-; and |p1f{-5/2}{+-1}~#|n2d{-5/2}, 
 86BRFcL J|p=0- to 5-, whereas medium energy excitations can involve |p1g{-9/2} 
 86BRGcL and |n1g{-7/2} orbitals with |p1g{-9/2}~#|n2d{-5/2}, J|p=2+ to 7+; and 
 86BRHcL |p1g{-9/2}~#|n2g{-7/2}, J|p=1+ to 8+ (2016Ur04)                        
