 86BR    86KR(T,3HEG)                  2019TI09                  25NDS    202507
 86BR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=A. Negret and B. Singh$CIT=NDS 203, 283 (2025)$            
 86BR2 H CUT=20-Jan-2025$                                                       
 86BR c  2019Ti09: E(t)=115 MeV/nucleon produced from fragmentation of a        
 86BR2c  primary {+16}O beam at 150 MeV/nucleon on a {+9}Be target, followed    
 86BR3c  by extraction of {+3}H ions using the A1900 fragment separator at the  
 86BR4c  NSCL-MSU facility. Reaction target was {+86}Kr gas at pressure of 1210 
 86BR5c  torr. Measured E|g, angular distributions from 0|' to 4|' in the c.m.  
 86BR6c  system, and ({+3}He)|g-coin using the GRETINA array of                 
 86BR7c  36-fold segmented, 32 HPGe crystals, and the S800 spectrograph.        
 86BR8c  FWHM |?400 keV for particles. Deduced cross sections for population of 
 86BR9c  states in {+86}Br, |DL values of transitions using multipole           
 86BRAc  decomposition analysis (MDA), Gamow-Teller transition strength from    
 86BRBc  {+86}Kr to {+86}Br, and stellar electron-capture rates based on the    
 86BRCc  extracted B(>) strengths. Comparison with shell-model and              
 86BRDc  quasiparticle random-phase approximation (QRPA) calculations.          
 86BR c  Gamow-Teller strength distributions extracted from this experiment up  
 86BR2c  to 5-MeV excitation energy are shown in Fig. 5 of 2019Ti09, with       
 86BR3c  comparison to shell-model and QRPA calculations using NUSHELLX code.   
 86BR cG E$Deduced by 2019Ti09 with a gate width of |?5 keV placed around each  
 86BR2cG |g-ray peak in the |g spectrum                                         
 86BR cL E$Deduced by 2019Ti09 from a gate width of |?1.5 MeV placed around each
 86BR2cL of the excitation energy peak in the excitation energy spectrum, with  
 86BR3cL uncertainty stated by authors as |?0.3 MeV                             
 86BR cL L$From multipole decomposition analysis (MDA) of angular distribution  
 86BR2cL data for excited states up to 5 MeV excitation energy (shown in Fig. 4 
 86BR3cL of 2019Ti09) associated with relevant |g-ray peaks, and the use of     
 86BR4cL DWBA code FOLD. All the values are listed as tentative by 2019Ti09     
