 86KR c  {+86}Kr isotope identified in mass spectroscopic studies by            
 86KR2c  1920As01, 1920As03, 1921As01, 1921As05, 1923As04, 1925As02, 1930As04,  
 86KR3c  and 1933Ba02.                                                          
 86KR c  Other reaction:                                                        
 86KR c  {+86}Kr(n,n) E|<1 MeV: 1989Jo01: analyzed |s(E) to deduce              
 86KR2c  optical model parameter.                                               
 86KR c  Mean square charge radius and isotopic shift: 2000Ga58, 1995Ke04,      
 86KR2c  1992Sc19, 1990Sc30, 1990Ca26, 1989Tr04, 1981Ge06, 1977Ge05             
 86KR c  Mass measurements: 1978Di09                                            
 86KR c  Theoretical nuclear structure calculations:                            
 86KR c  2023Zh37: calculated g.s. proprieties (binding energy, deformation,    
 86KR2c  charge radius) for Kr and Sr isotopes within the deformed relativistic 
 86KR3c  Hartree-Bogoliubov theory.                                             
 86KR c  2022Ka19: calculated triaxial quadrupole potential energy surfaces,    
 86KR2c  energies and collective wave functions contours in (|b,|g) planes for  
 86KR3c  the low-lying positive-parity states, ratios of level energies, B(E2), 
 86KR4c  properties of E0 transitions, fluctuations of |b and |g deformations   
 86KR5c  using triaxial quadrupole constrained self-consistent mean-field (SCMF)
 86KR6c  theory with DD-ME2 and DD-PC1 relativistic energy density functionals  
 86KR7c  and pairing interaction.                                               
 86KR c  2018No06, 2017No08: calculated deformation energy surfaces in (|b,|g)  
 86KR2c  plane, levels, J|p, excited 0+ stated, B(E2) and spectroscopic         
 86KR3c  quadrupole moments of the first 2+ states using interacting            
 86KR4c  boson-fermion model (IBFM) with Gogny-D1M energy density functional.   
 86KR c  2017Ab09: calculated potential energy surfaces (PES) in (|b{-2},|g)    
 86KR2c  planes using triaxial relativistic-Hartree-Bogoliubov (RHB) formalism  
 86KR3c  with DD-PC1 and DD-ME2 parameter sets, binding energy, neutron and     
 86KR4c  proton radii, rms charge radii, S(2n) using relativistic               
 86KR5c  Hartree-Bogoliubov formalism with density-dependent zero and finite    
 86KR6c  range NN interactions, and separable pairing force.                    
 86KR c  2016Ur04: calculated levels, J|p, occupation of neutron and proton     
 86KR2c  orbitals using large-scale shell-model with the coupled-scheme code    
 86KR3c  NATHAN, in valence space outside the inert {+78}Ni core: |p1f{-5/2},   
 86KR4c  |p2p{-3/2}, |p2p{-1/2}, and |p1g{-9/2} proton orbitals; and |n2d{-5/2},
 86KR4c  |n3s{-1/2}, |n1g{-7/2}, |n2d{-3/2}, and |n1h{-11/2} neutron orbitals.  
 86KR c  2014Ro21: calculated potential energy surfaces contours in (|b{-2},|g) 
 86KR2c  plane, neutron single-particle energies as function of |b{-2}          
 86KR3c  parameter, wave function contours for low-lying 0+ and 2+ levels in    
 86KR4c  (|b{-2},|g) plane, positive-parity levels up to 8+, quasi |g bands,    
 86KR5c  B(E2), |r{+2}(E0), quadrupole moments, g factors, shape transitions    
 86KR6c  and shape coexistence using self-consistent beyond-mean-field,         
 86KR7c  symmetry-conserving configuration mixing (SCCM) methods with Gogny D1S 
 86KR8c  interaction.                                                           
 86KR c  2014Za10: calculated orbital and spin g factors of the first 2+ and 4+ 
 86KR2c  states by surface delta interaction (SDI) approach, and large-scale    
 86KR3c  shell model wave functions for 2+ and 4+ states.                       
 86KR c  2013Fu06: calculated levels, J|p, energy surface contours in |b-|g     
 86KR2c  plane, B(E2), |r{+2}(E0), quadrupole deformation,                      
 86KR3c  oblate-triaxial-prolate transition, shape coexistence, configuration   
 86KR4c  mixing, angular momentum projection using beyond relativistic          
 86KR5c  mean-field (RMF) theory with |a(P)-PK1 force.                          
 86KR c  2012Si08: calculated levels, J|p, monopole effects using shell-model   
 86KR2c  in a large model space of {Ipf} for protons, and {Ifpgd} for neutrons. 
 86KR c  2006Ka39: calculated levels, J|p, B(E2), configurations, shell closure 
 86KR2c  features using shell-model and mean-field method.                      
 86KR c  2003Me26: calculated 2+ energy, g factors, pair gaps, deformation,     
 86KR2c  B(E2) using interacting boson model, pairing-corrected collective      
 86KR3c  model, and shell model.                                                
 86KR c  1995La07: calculated binding energy, rms charge, neutron radii, isotope
 86KR2c  shifts, neutron skin thickness, shape coexistence, quadrupole          
 86KR3c  deformation using relativistic mean field theory.                      
 86KR c  1995Re19: calculated levels, J|p, B(|l) using shell model.             
 86KR c  1992Si14: calculated levels, J|p, B(|l) using shell model.             
 86KR c  1989Ji06, 1988Ji04, 1988Xi01: calculated levels, binding energy, single
 86KR2c  nucleon transfer spectroscopic factors using shell model.              
 86KR c  1987Ha21: calculated levels, J|p, quadrupole moments, B(|l), potential 
 86KR2c  energy surfaces using interacting boson model.                         
 86KR c  1982Ah06: calculated yrast band B(E2), quadrupole moments using        
 86KR2c  projected Hartree-Fock method with Kuo-Brown interaction.              
 86KR c  1982Br01: calculated levels, J|p, B(E2), two-nucleon transfer          
 86KR2c  probabilities using nuclear field theory (NFT) version of the pair     
 86KR3c  aligned model.                                                         
 86KR c  1981Bu06: calculated potential energy surfaces, shape phase transition,
 86KR2c  shell and pairing effect microscopic corrections using macroscopic     
 86KR3c  approach.                                                              
