 86KR c  2018He09: Unsafe Coulomb excitation in inverse kinematics.             
 86KR2c  Beam={+86}Kr at 256.7 MeV from TRIUMF-ISAC facility.                   
 86KR2c  Target=carbon 0.5 mg/cm{+2} thick backed on 28.8 mg/cm{+2} Au foil.    
 86KR3c  Measured E|g, (particle)|g-coin, and level lifetimes by Doppler-shift  
 86KR4c  attenuation method (DSAM) using TIGRESS array of 11 {I32}-fold         
 86KR5c  segmented HPGe detectors for |g detection, and TIGRESS plunger device  
 86KR6c  (TIPS) consisting of a wall of 24 CsI(Tl) detectors for particle       
 86KR7c  detection. Monte Carlo simulations used for extraction of level        
 86KRxc  lifetimes.                                                             
 86KR c  2014Ku10: The g-factors of excited states were measured using the      
 86KR2c  transient-field (TF) technique in Coulomb excitation in inverse        
 86KR3c  kinematics with perturbed angular correlation (PAC) method.            
 86KR4c  Isotopically pure {+86}Kr beams with energy of 3.0, 3.1 and 3.2        
 86KR5c  MeV/nucleon and average intensity of |?1 pnA were delivered by the     
 86KR6c  K500 Texas A&M University (TAMU) cyclotron. The multilayered target    
 86KR7c  consisted of C, Gd, Ta, and Cu with the coulomb excitation occurring   
 86KR8c  in the carbon layer. Additional copper foils of 5.6 mg/cm{+2} were     
 86KR9c  placed behind the target and in front of the particle detector to      
 86KRAc  prevent the beam from reaching the detector. The target was mounted    
 86KRBc  on the tip of a Displex Closed Cycle refrigerator, which serves as     
 86KRCc  one pole piece of an electromagnet with an external magnetic field of  
 86KRDc  0.07 T with field direction reversed every 130 s. The target was kept  
 86KREc  at approximately 50 Kelvin. The detection system consisted of four     
 86KRFc  Clover HPGe |g detectors, and a PIPS Canberra Si surface barrier       
 86KRGc  particle detector. Measured |a, |g, |a|g coin, (particle)|g(|q),       
 86KRHc  and g-factors.                                                         
 86KR c  2001Me20: {+26}Mg({+86}Kr,{+86}Kr'),E({+86}Kr)=220-261 MeV. Measured   
