 86KR c  2013Fo13: A neutron beam with energy ranging from 1-20 MeV was         
 86KR2c  produced in a W spallation target driven by a E(p)=800 MeV beam at the 
 86KR3c  LANSCE WNR facility of LANL. The neutron beam impinged on a            
 86KR4c  0.525 mm thick aluminum target cylinder containing {+86}Kr gas at      
 86KR5c  P=450 kPa. The cylinder had a length of 6.261 cm and a radius of 1.7975
 86KR6c  cm. Measured E|g, I|g, |s, |g|g-coin using the GEANIE spectrometer     
 86KR7c  consisting of 10 Compton-suppressed planar Ge detectors, and 10        
 86KR8c  Compton-suppressed coaxial Ge detectors. Deduced levels, J, |p.        
 86KR9c  Comparison with shell-model calculations.                              
