 86RB  Q 1776.10   20 8650.9820 8555.6 20-7673.2 10    2021WA16                 
 86RB cQ $S(2n)=19130.7 {I22}, S(2p)=19542 {I26} (2021Wa16)                     
 86RB c  {+86}Rb first produced by 1937Sn02, later confirmed by 1941He02.       
 86RB2c  The 1-min isomer was identified by 1951Fl17                            
 86RB c  Mass measurement: 1994Ot01 (Penning-Trap method)                       
 86RB c  2015Im02: measured hyperfine structure (HFS) resonance spectra; deduced
 86RB2c  feasibility of hyperfine splitting and magnetic moments measurements.  
 86RB c  2014Ya28: measured laser-radio-frequency double-resonance spectra using
 86RB2c  superfluid helium at 1.8|' K at the RIKEN projectile fragment separator
 86RB3c  (RIPS) facility, deduced spin from measured Zeeman splitting.          
 86RB d  2001Sa27: {+87}Rb(n,2n) E=13.4-14.9 MeV. Measured cross section        
 86RB c  Theoretical structure calculations:                                    
 86RB c  2018Qi05: calculated energy surfaces as function of deformation        
 86RB2c  parameter |b, triaxiality deformation parameters |g and |b, total      
 86RB3c  energies and excitation energies for various valence nucleon           
 86RB4c  configurations, chiral partner bands using adiabatic and               
 86RB5c  configuration-fixed constrained triaxial relativistic mean-field theory
 86RB c  2015Et01: calculated levels, J|p, unperturbed energies of              
 86RB2c  neutron-proton 2-qp states using empirical core-particle coupling model
 86RB3c  with Skyrme-QRPA approach.                                             
 86RB c  2015Is09: calculated electric quadrupole moments and reduced transition
 86RB2c  rates for E2 transition, magnetic moments, systematics of low-lying    
 86RB3c  positive-parity levels using two-group shell model.                    
 86RB c  2009Ho14: calculated levels, J|p, and transition matrix elements using 
 86RB2c  shell model                                                            
 86RB c  1987My01: calculated rms charge radii, deformations, potential energy  
 86RB2c  surfaces, collective quadrupole zero-point motion contribution.        
 86RB d  Other theory references for structure: 2021Co17, 2018Bu13, 2016Du17,   
 86RB2d  2008Ga20, 1987He15, 1981Ga20, 1975Fu11.                                
 86RB cG E,RI$From (n,|g) and ({+7}Li,3n|g). In (n,|g), several tentative       
 86RB2cG placements of secondary transitions are not shown here.                
 86RB3cG See (n,|g) dataset for details.                                        
 86RB cG M$From |g(|q), |g|g(|q)(DCO) and |g(lin pol) in ({+7}Li,3n|g)          
 86RB cL $There are 290 neutron resonances known from E(n)(lab)=175.6 eV to     
 86RB2cL 19.08 keV, corresponding to excitation energy range of 8651.2 to       
 86RB3cL 8669.9 keV.                                                            
 86RB cL $Low-lying negative-parity states are expected to be members of the    
 86RB3cL |p2p{-3/2}{+-1}~#|n1g{-9/2}{+-1} and                                   
 86RB4cL |p1f{-5/2}{+-1}~#|n1g{-9/2}{+-1} multiplets.                           
 86RB5cL Since {+87}Rb g.s. configuration=|p2p{-3/2}{+-1}~#|p1f{-5/2}{++6}      
 86RB6cL and {+85}Rb g.s. configuration=|p2p{-3/2}{++4}~#|p1f{-5/2}{+-1},       
 86RB7cL the first multiplet is expected to be strongly populated in            
 86RB8cL {+87}Rb({+3}He,|a) and {+87}Rb(d,t) reactions, whereas the second      
 86RB9cL multiplet is expected to be populated in {+85}Rb(d,p). States belonging
 86RBAcL to the first multiplet have been identified with reasonable certainty  
 86RBBcL and are in agreement with shell-model calculations (1969Da15), whereas 
 86RBCcL the members of the second multiplet cannot be identified unambiguously.
 86RBDcL For further remarks see 1969Da15, 1972Ho44, 1972Ko37, 1977HeYQ, and    
 86RBEcL 1975Du02 (for configuration mixing effects).                           
 86RB cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g values wherever possible. See          
 86RB2cL ({+3}He,p) for some additional tentative levels and associated         
 86RBxcL L-transfers                                                            
 86RB cL E(d)$Possible doublet from neutron-resonance data (2018MuZY)           
 86RB cL J$Primary |g from 2-,3- limits J|p to 0- to 5-. For high-spin          
 86RB2cL states, positive parity is from systematics while negative parity      
 86RB3cL is from a comparison with shell-model calculations                     
 86RB cL J(r)$From analysis of neutron-resonance data (2018MuZY)                
 86RB cL T$From DSAM in {+82}Se({+7}Li,3n|g), except as noted otherwise.        
 86RB CL BAND(A)$Yrast band.                                                    
 86RB CL BAND(C)$Negative parity band.                                          
