 86SR c  Other reactions:                                                       
 86SR c  {+85}Rb(p,n): IAR. Six resonances reported. See {+85}Rb(p,n) dataset   
 86SR c  {+86}Sr(d,d): 1968Ko20                                                 
 86SR c  {+86}Sr(t,t): 1970Ra10                                                 
 86SR c  Measurements of isotope shifts, hyperfine structure, radii, etc.:      
 86SR c  1992Ba55, 1991As06, 1990Bu12 (also 1988Si06), 1987Ea01, 1987An02,      
 86SR2c  1986Ma43, 1986An39, 1985Bu20, 1984Be44, 1983Lo13, 1983El04,            
 86SR3c  1983Bo35, 1981Be42, 1961He18                                           
 86SR c  {+88}Sr({+12}C,{+14}C) E=87.5 MeV: 1995Ro11, Measured |s(|q),          
 86SR2c  deduced reaction mechanisms.                                           
 86SR c  {+92}Mo(n,X) E=2-250 MeV: 2000Ga46, measured excitation function       
 86SR2c  for {+86}Sr yield through the intensity of |g ray from the             
 86SR3c  first excited state                                                    
 86SR c  Theoretical nuclear structure calculations:                            
 86SR c  2024Ni08: calculated g.s. and charge radius within a binary cluster    
 86SR2c  model                                                                  
 86SR c  2023Zh37: calculated g.s. proprieties (binding energy, deformation,    
 86SR2c  charge radius) for Kr and Sr isotopes within the deformed relativistic 
 86SR3c  Hartree-Bogoliubov theory.                                             
 86SR c  2017Ab09: calculated potential energy surfaces in (|b{-2},|g) plane,   
 86SR2c  two ground-state minima, binding energy, neutron and proton radii,     
 86SR3c  rms charge radius, S(2n) using relativistic Hartree-Bogoliubov         
 86SR4c  formalism with density-dependent zero and finite range nucleon-nucleon 
 86SR5c  interactions, and separable pairing force.                             
 86SR c  2015Sa26: calculated low-lying energy levels, J|p, energies of quasi-|g
 86SR2c  and quasi-|b bands, B(E2), g-factors using interacting boson model.    
 86SR c  2014Zh43: calculated deformation parameters |b{-2} and |g using        
 86SR2c  nonaxial deformed Woods-Saxon (WS) potential, and pairing by           
 86SR3c  Lipkin-Nogami approach.                                                
 86SR c  2013Ti03: calculated rms charge radius, S(2n), three-point neutron     
 86SR2c  pairing energy of ground state using density functional theory with    
 86SR3c  DD-PC1 parameter set.                                                  
 86SR c  2010Ro17: calculated charge radius, S(n), deformation using HFB method 
 86SR2c  based on Gogny-D1S interaction.                                        
 86SR c  2006Be63: calculated neutron subshell energies, and occupation         
 86SR2c  probabilities using dispersive optical model.                          
 86SR c  2006Zh41: calculated neutron and proton shell gaps, total energy per   
 86SR2c  nucleon, quadrupole deformation, isotope shifts, shape coexistence,    
 86SR3c  S(2n) using relativistic mean-field theory with density-dependent |d   
 86SR4c  interaction.                                                           
 86SR c  2003Me26: calculated energy of 2+ state, g-factor, pairing gap,        
 86SR2c  deformation, B(E2) using interacting boson model, pairing-corrected    
 86SR3c  collective model, and shell model.                                     
 86SR c  1997Su08: calculated energies of ground- and |g-bands using            
 86SR2c  interacting boson model.                                               
 86SR c  1995Ba45: calculated rms radius, neutron and proton radii,             
 86SR2c  quadrupole deformations, quadrupole moments using mean field approach. 
 86SR c  1995Ba78: calculated binding energy per particle vs deformation,       
 86SR2c  isotope shifts, level energies vs deformation using constrained        
 86SR3c  Hartree-Fock approach.                                                 
 86SR c  1995La07: calculated binding energy, rms charge, neutron radius,       
 86SR2c  isotope shifts, neutron skin thickness, shape coexistence, quadrupole  
 86SR3c  deformation using relativistic mean field theory.                      
 86SR c  1993He12: calculated levels, J|p, isotope shifts, binding energy       
 86SR2c  using generator coordinate method.                                     
 86SR c  1993Hi11: calculated binding energy per particle, isotope shifts       
 86SR2c  using relativistic mean field theory.                                  
 86SR c  1993Ku19: calculated variations of mean square charge radius using     
 86SR2c  RPA approach; discussed role of dynamic effects.                       
 86SR c  1991Bo27: calculated ground state energy, probability densities,       
 86SR2c  levels, J|p, isotope shifts, potential energy surfaces using generator 
 86SR3c  coordinate method.                                                     
 86SR c  1984He07: calculated levels, J|p, quadrupole moments, isotope and      
 86SR2c  isomer shifts using interacting boson model.                           
 86SR c  1979Bu20: calculated potential energy surfaces, ground-state           
 86SR2c  equilibrium deformation using Strutinsky shell correction method with  
 86SR3c  pairing effects.                                                       
 86SR c  1973Og01: calculated levels, J|p using shell model.                    
 86SR c  1971Ki16: calculated levels, J|p, one-nucleon spectroscopic factors    
 86SR2c  wave functions using shell model with effective interaction.           
 86SR c  Other theory references for structure: 50 references retrieved from    
 86SR2c  the NSR database are listed in this dataset as 'document' records.     
 86SR d  Other theory references for structure: 2022Al15, 2022An05, 2022Bo16,   
