 86SR    76GE(13C,3NG)                 2016KU17,2017KU04         25NDS    202507
 86SR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=A. Negret and B. Singh$CIT=NDS 203, 283 (2025)$            
 86SR2 H CUT=20-Jan-2025$                                                       
 86SR c  2016Ku17, 2017Ku04: E({+13}C)=45 MeV. Target=850 |mg/cm{+2} {+76}Ge    
 86SR2c  on a backing of 7.6 mg/cm{+2} thick {+181}Ta. Measured E|g, I|g,       
 86SR3c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO), |g|g(linear pol), and lifetimes of levels in 
 86SR4c  the |DJ=1 band by DSAM using the INGA array of 15 Compton-suppressed   
 86SR5c  Clover HPGe detectors at Pelletron facility of TIFR. Two- and          
 86SR6c  three-dimensional |g|g-coin matrices were generated with a time window 
 86SR7c  of 200 ns. Deduced high-spin levels, J, |p, multipolarities, bands and 
 86SR8c  configurations. Comparison with shell-model and TAC calculations.      
 86SR9c  Main spectroscopic studies are reported in 2016Ku17 while lifetimes    
 86SRAc  in 2017Ku04.                                                           
 86SR cG $DCO ratios correspond to 90|' and 157|' geometry with gates on        
 86SR2cG |DJ=2, quadrupole transitions or |DJ=1, dipole transitions.            
 86SR3cG Expected DCO values are: 1.0 for |DJ=2, quadrupole and 0.52 for |DJ=1, 
 86SR4cG dipole when gated on |DJ=2, quadrupole. 1.0 for |DJ=1, dipole and 1.92 
 86SR5cG for |DJ=2, quadrupole when gated on |DJ=1, dipole. The gates are on    
 86SR6cG 303.8, 476.2, 821.9, 1076.6, 1752.8 transitions; 821.9|g,              
 86SR7cG 1076.6|g and 1752.8|g are |DJ=2, quadrupole transitions; and           
 86SR8cG 303.8|g, 476.2|g are |DJ=1, dipole.                                    
 86SR cG $DCO(Q) is DCO value for gate on |DJ=2, quadrupole transition,         
 86SR2cG and DCO(D) for |DJ=1, dipole transition                                
