 86SR c  2014Li25, 2015Zh18: E({+9}Be)=40-53 MeV. Target=0.85 mg/cm{+2} thick   
 86SR2c  enriched {+82}Se foil with 4.5 mg/cm{+2} thick gold backing. Measured  
 86SR3c  E|g, I|g, excitation functions at E=40, 44, 46, 48, 52 and 53 MeV,     
 86SR4c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO) using an array of nine BGO-Compton suppressed 
 86SR5c  HPGe detectors, one Clover Ge detector, and two planar HPGe detectors  
 86SR6c  at CIAE's HI-13 tandem accelerator facility. Deduced levels, J, |p,    
 86SR7c  multipolarity, particle configurations. Comparison with detailed       
 86SR8c  shell-model calculations, assuming {+56}Ni as an inert core and        
 86SR9c  1f{-5/2}, 2p{-3/2}, 2p{-1/2} and 1g{-9/2} orbitals for proton and      
 86SRAc  neutron excitations.                                                   
 86SRBc  2014Li25 and 2015Zh18 present the results from the same measurement,   
 86SRCc  but in 2015Zh18 an additional sequence is identified as a              
 86SRDc  magnetic-dipole rotational band based on the 6879.9-keV level.         
 86SR cG $DCO data are for 40|' and 90|' geometry. DCO(D) and DCO(Q) are for    
 86SR2cG gates on stretched dipole and stretched quadrupole transitions,        
 86SR3cG respectively. Expected DCO ratios are: 1.6 for stretched quadrupole and
 86SR4cG 1.0 for stretched dipole when gated on stretched dipole; 1.0 for       
 86SR5cG stretched quadrupole and 0.7 for stretched dipole when gated on        
 86SR6cG stretched quadrupole.                                                  
 86SR cG E$2014Li25, 2015Zh18 state uncertainty of 0.2-0.5 keV depending on     
 86SR2cG intensity. Evaluators assign 0.2 keV for I|g>15, 0.3 keV for I|g=5-15, 
 86SR3cG and 0.5 keV for I|g<5, and when I|g not given                          
 86SR cG RI$At E({+9}Be)=53 MeV                                                 
