 86ZR    86NB EC DECAY (88 S)          1985WA10                  25NDS    202507
 86ZR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=A. Negret and B. Singh$CIT=NDS 203, 283 (2025)$            
 86ZR2 H CUT=20-Jan-2025$                                                       
 86ZR c  The activities studied by 1985Wa10 and 1994Sh07 may be composed        
 86ZR2c  of at least two isomers of {+86}Nb: one of the isomers is the known    
 86ZR3c  88-s activity (J|p=(6+)), the other may be a low-spin isomer           
 86ZR4c  which may feed low-spin states in {+86}Zr. Since the 56-s isomer has   
 86ZR5c  not been confirmed in more recent studies of 1997Ta10 (2000DoZV)       
 86ZR6c  and 2005Ka39, evaluators assume that the main activity is from         
 86ZR7c  88-s, (6+) {+86}Nb decay, although, contribution from a possible       
 86ZR8c  isomer in {+86}Nb is possible                                          
 86ZR c  1985Wa10: Source produced by {+58}Ni({+32}S,3pn|g).                    
 86ZR2c  Measured E|g, I|g, (x ray)|g(t), |g|g(t), |b|g(t).                     
 86ZR c  1994Sh07 report another {+86}Nb |e decay (56.3 s). Source produced by  
 86ZR2c  {+54}Fe({+35}Cl,2pn|g), E=103 MeV; (x ray)|g coin gated on the 752, 914
 86ZR3c  and 1003 keV |g rays and decay curve.                                  
 86ZR c  Others: 1977Ko05, 1982De43, 1974Vo03.                                  
 86ZR c  Comments from 2000DoZV suggest observing 50 additional transitions     
 86ZR2c  in this decay, some of these populate high spin states such as         
 86ZR3c  3272, 6-; 3424 and 3647, both 7-; 3298 and 3533, both 8+. Although     
 86ZR4c  details of this study are not available, it would seem, however,       
 86ZR5c  that the level scheme is much more complex than that proposed by       
 86ZR6c  1985Wa10. For this reason, %|e+%|b{++} feedings and associated log|    
 86ZR7c  {Ift} values (as given by 1985Wa10) were not reproduced here. In       
 86ZR8c  addition there is still a large gap between the Q(|b{+-})value and the 
 86ZR9c  top excitation energy known from the study of 1985Wa10. Contribution   
 86ZRAc  from possible different isomers of {+86}Nb (although only one is       
 86ZRBc  firmly established so far, but at least one other low-spin             
 86ZRCc  isomer is also expected) would further complicate the issue.           
 86ZR c  The decay scheme is incomplete since many transitions remain unobserved
 86ZR2c  or unreported. No normalization can be meaningfully done.              
 86ZR cG RI(A)$Contamination intensity subtracted.                              
