 86NB cL E$evaluators assume 88-s, (6+) activity as the g.s., although a strict 
 86NB2cL evidence for its assignment to g.s. is lacking                         
 86NB cL J$from systematics and in-beam experiments (1997Ta10,1999Co10).        
 86NB2cL J|p=5+ proposed earlier is not supported by more recent                
 86NB3cL experiments (2000DoZV). No 6+ to 5+ transition is seen by 1997Ta10     
 86NB cL T$from 1985Wa10. Others: 87 s {I3} (1982De43), 80 s {I12} (1977Ko05),  
 86NB2cL 84 s {I12} (1974Vo03) are all in agreement but less precise            
