 86NB c  2005Ka39: {+86}Mo produced by a 150-170 MeV {+32}S beam impinging on a 
 86NB2c  {+nat}Ni target. The reaction products were separated using the IGISOL 
 86NB3c  facility and implanted into a collector tape. Two HPGe detectors and a 
 86NB4c  plastic scintillator were placed next to the implantation position and 
 86NB5c  two low-energy Ge detectors and a magnetic conversion-electron         
 86NB6c  spectrometer (ELLI) were placed at a second detector station. Measured 
 86NB7c  E|g, I|g, |g|g coin, conversion electrons.                             
 86NB c  1994Sh07: {+86}Mo produced in reactions {+54}Fe({+35}Cl,p2n|g)         
 86NB2c  E=103 MeV, and {+58}Ni({+32}S,2p2n|g) E=120 MeV;                       
 86NB3c  identification by (x ray)|g- and |b|g coin and cross bombardment.      
 86NB c  The decay scheme of {+86}Mo to {+86}Nb does not seem complete in view  
 86NB2c  of possible missing higher levels (above the currently known level at  
 86NB3c  236+x) and high Q value, thus I|g/100 decays, |e feedings and log|     
 86NB4c  {Ift} values cannot be deduced                                         
 86NB c  Theory for decay of {+86}Mo: 2011Sa06, 1992Bi07                        
