 86MO c  First half-life measurement of {+86}Mo isotope was made by 1994Sh07 in 
 86MO2c  {+54}Fe({+35}Cl,p2n|g),E=103 MeV; {+58}Ni({+32}S,2p2n|g),E=120 MeV     
 86MO3c  reactions and identified by (x ray)|g and |b|g coincidences and        
 86MO4c  cross-bombardment. First identification of {+86}Mo was by 1991Gr18 in  
 86MO5c  in-beam |g-ray studies using {+40}Ca({+50}Cr,2p2n|g),E=170 MeV;        
 86MO6c  and {+58}Ni({+32}S,2p2n|g),E=110 MeV reactions and employing recoil-|g 
 86MO7c  and |g|g-coin technique.                                               
 86MO c  2015Al19: isotopic yield and cross section measurements in             
 86MO2c  {+2}H({+136}Xe,X),E=500 MeV/nucleon at GSI facility                    
 86MO c  Mass measurement: 2019Vi05                                             
 86MO c  Theoretical structure calculations:                                    
 86MO c  2024Ag02: calculated deformation parameters and separation energies,   
 86MO2c  investigated shape coexistence using the Nilsson Strutinsky            
 86MO3c  Method and the Relativistic Mean Field Model.                          
 86MO c  2021Th08: calculated potential energy curves, shell closure parameters,
 86MO2c  S(2n), root mean square radius, neutron skin thickness using density   
 86MO3c  dependent meson exchange model DD-ME2 and density dependent point      
 86MO4c  coupling models DD-PC1 and DD-PCX.                                     
 86MO c  2021Sa48: calculated proton-proton, neutron-neutron and proton-neutron 
 86MO2c  pairing gaps using the deformed Bardeen-Cooper-Schriefer (DBCS) theory.
 86MO c  2017Ka01: calculated deformation, spin, quadrupole moment, yrast bands,
 86MO2c  B(E2) using state-of-the-art shell model.                              
 86MO c  2017El01: calculated binding energy, mass excess, S(n), S(2n), charge  
 86MO2c  and neutron radii, neutron pairing gap, quadrupole deformation using   
 86MO3c  HFB method with SLy4 Skyrme force.                                     
 86MO c  2015Bh13: calculated binding energy, root-mean-square charge radius,   
 86MO2c  quadrupole deformation parameter |b{-2} for the ground states and      
 86MO3c  selected first few intrinsic excited states using relativistic         
 86MO4c  mean-field formalism with NL3 and NL3* forces.                         
 86MO c  2014Eb02: calculated low-lying electric dipole (E1) strengths of pygmy 
 86MO2c  dipole resonances (PDR), the PDR fraction as functions of the neutron  
 86MO3c  number and neutron skin thickness, proton number dependence of the PDR 
 86MO4c  fraction, shell structure, neutron skin thickness, neutron and proton  
 86MO5c  pairing gaps and chemical potentials, quadrupole deformation parameters
 86MO6c  |b{-2} and |g using canonical-basis time-dependent                     
 86MO7c  Hartree-Fock-Bogoliubov (Cb-TDHFB) theory                              
 86MO c  2014Zh43: calculated total-Routhian surface energies, kinetic moments  
 86MO2c  of inertia with prolate, oblate, and triaxial deformations using       
 86MO3c  nonaxial deformed Woods-Saxon (WS) potential, and pairing by           
 86MO4c  Lipkin-Nogami approach.                                                
 86MO c  2012Bh10: calculated S(2n), |b{-2}, S(p), binding energy using         
 86MO2c  microscopic-macroscopic model with Wigner-Kirkwood expansion.          
 86MO c  2011Ro50: calculated binding energy, and charge radius using           
 86MO2c  relativistic Brueckner theory, high-precision density functional       
 86MO3c  with density-dependent meson-nucleon couplings.                        
 86MO c  2002Ma30: calculated moments of inertia for rotational bands           
 86MO2c  using Projected shell model.                                           
 86MO c  2010Pr02: calculated energy levels, J|p, B(E2) using general Bohr      
 86MO2c  collective model, and the Skyrme effective interaction.                
 86MO c  2008Af02: calculated moments of inertia, proton density, single        
 86MO2c  particle orbital energy gaps using cranked relativistic mean-field     
 86MO3c  theory.                                                                
 86MO c  2004Su08: calculated deformations, rotational bands moments of inertia 
 86MO2c  using projected shell model.                                           
 86MO c  1993Ki04: calculated nucleon occupation numbers, role of neutron-proton
 86MO2c  interaction in deformation using Hartree-Fock-Bogolyubov approach.     
 86MO c  1993Lu10: calculated total Routhian energy surfaces using cranking     
 86MO2c  approximation by Strutinsky method.                                    
 86MO c  1992Bi07: calculated T{-1/2} of {+86}Mo decay using random phase       
 86MO2c  approximation and quasiparticle formalism.                             
 86MO c  Other theoretical structure references: 15 references in the           
 86MO2c  NSR database listed in this dataset as 'document' records.             
