 86RU c  2017Su26, 2013Su23: {+86}Ru nuclide identified in {+9}Be({+124}Xe,X),  
 86RU2c  E({+124}Xe)=345 MeV/nucleon beam produced by the cascade operation of  
 86RU3c  the RIBF accelerator complex of the linear accelerators RILAC and      
 86RU4c  RILAC-II and the four cyclotrons, RRC, fRC, IRC, and SRC.              
 86RU5c  Identification of {+86}Ru nuclei was made on the basis of magnetic     
 86RU6c  rigidity, time-of-flight and energy loss (tof-B|r-|DE method) of the   
 86RU7c  fragments using BigRIPS fragment separator, atomic number Z of fragment
 86RU8c  by tof and |DE, and A/Q (atomic mass/charge state) of fragment by B|r  
 86RU9c  and tof. Time-of-flight was measured using thin plastic                
 86RUAc  scintillators, |DE by MUSIC ionization chambers, and B|r by particle   
 86RUBc  trajectory reconstructions. Experiments were performed at              
 86RUCc  RIBF-RIKEN facility. Measured A/Q versus Z distributions, deduced      
 86RUDc  production cross sections. Theoretical calculations were performed     
 86RUEc  using fission model based LISE** code, and empirical calculations      
 86RUFc  were made using EPAX3.01 and EPAX2.15 codes.                           
 86RU c  Theoretical structure calculations:                                    
 86RU c  2024Ag02: calculated deformation parameters and separation energies,   
 86RU2c  investigated shape coexistence using the Nilsson Strutinsky            
 86RU3c  Method and the Relativistic Mean Field Model.                          
 86RU c  2017El01: calculated binding energy, mass excess, S(n), S(2n), charge  
 86RU2c  and neutron radii, neutron pairing gap, quadrupole deformation using   
 86RU3c  HFB method with SLy4 Skyrme force.                                     
 86RU c  2015Bh13: calculated binding energy, root-mean-square charge radius,   
 86RU2c  quadrupole deformation parameter |b{-2} for the ground states and      
 86RU3c  few intrinsic excited states using relativistic mean-field formalism   
 86RU4c  with NL3 and NL3* forces.                                              
 86RU c  1997He24: calculated binding energy, T{-1/2} using shell model.        
 86RU c  Other theoretical structure references: seven references in the        
 86RU2c  NSR database listed in this dataset as 'document' records.             
 86RU d  Other theoretical calculations: 2022Ca20, 2022Zo01, 2021Kl02,          
 86RU2d  2019Zo02, 2015Wu04, 2008Sc02, 2003St22.                                
